4.Subject to the provisions of this Act and any otherwritten law, the Foundation shall have the power–

(a) to request and receive contributions, grants,donations and gifts of all forms as may be necessaryfor the purpose of the Foundation;

(b) to purchase, rent, lease or otherwise obtain lands orbuildings which may be required for the purpose ofthe Foundation;

(c) to borrow or raise funds with or without interest forthe purposes of the Foundation;

(d) to make, draw, accept, discount, endorse, buy, selland issue bills of exchange, cheques, promissorynotes and other negotiable instruments and to open,operate, maintain and close accounts in any bank;

(e) to invest any funds that are not immediately requiredfor the purposes of the Foundation, in such manneras the Executive Council may deem necessary;

(f) to enter into agreement or contracts with any personor any company or body of persons with a view topromoting the objects of the Foundation;

